{"book":11,"chapter":31,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / JAVASCRIPT IN NODE.JS / CHAPTER 23","slides":[{"title":"Not just Node","sub":"Chapter 31 · Runtimes","short":"Intro","main":"Node, Deno and Bun are different runtimes for one language: standard JS is portable, platform APIs are not.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One runtime","Three runtimes","What we compare"],"captions":["For a long time Node was the only way to run JavaScript outside the browser","Now there are three: Node.js, Deno (Ryan Dahl) and Bun (speed and a toolkit)","Security, TypeScript, web standards, speed, maturity — and portable code"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":140.0,"h":50.0,"text":"Node.js","tone":"green","size":14.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":44.0,"text":"Node.js","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":44.0,"text":"Deno","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":44.0,"text":"Bun","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"security","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"TypeScript","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"web standards","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":120.0,"y":104.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"speed","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":240.0,"y":104.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"maturity","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.1,26.1]}]},{"title":"Deno","sub":"Secure by default","short":"Deno","main":"Deno: TypeScript with no setup, web standards, imports by URL and JSR, permissions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["TypeScript at once","Modules","No access"],"captions":["deno run app.ts — no compiling and no build config","Import by address or from JSR; standard library built on web standards","By default no files, no network, no environment: grant permissions with flags"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ deno run app.ts","","const n: number = 42;","console.log(n);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["import { join } from \"jsr:@std/path\";","import { serve } from \"https://example.com/m.ts\";"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":90.0,"y":80.0,"w":110.0,"h":44.0,"text":"script","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":290.0,"y":46.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"files ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"network ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":290.0,"y":114.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"env ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.6,25.1]}]},{"title":"Deno permissions","sub":"Flags and scopes","short":"Permissions","main":"--allow-read=/data permits only that path; --deny-* forbids selectively.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Scope","Network and env","deny wins"],"captions":["--allow-read=/data permits reading only inside /data","--allow-net=api.example.com and --allow-env=HOME — narrow permissions","--deny-* beats --allow-*; least privilege is good practice"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["deno run --allow-read=/data app.ts","","read(\"/data/a.txt\")   // ✓","read(\"/etc/passwd\")   // ✗"],"hl":[2],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["--allow-net=api.example.com","--allow-env=HOME,PATH"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["--allow-net","--deny-net=evil.example","// evil.example → denied, others OK"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.0,24.0]}]},{"title":"Bun","sub":"Speed, all in one","short":"Bun","main":"Bun: faster startup and package manager, built-in bundler and test runner, Node compatibility.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["All in one","Engine","Compatibility"],"captions":["One program: runtime, package manager, bundler, test runner","JavaScriptCore from Apple and fast startup; Bun.serve is a built-in server","Most Node packages and modules work; rare differences need checking"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"bun","tone":"yellow","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":30.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"runtime","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":30.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"pm","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":70.0,"y":120.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"bundler","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":290.0,"y":120.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"test","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["Bun.serve({","  port: 3000,","  fetch(req) { return new Response(\"hi\"); },","});"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Node modules:\nmostly work","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"rare differences:\ncheck yourself","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.1,26.1]}]},{"title":"Shared standards","sub":"One API for all","short":"Standards","main":"fetch, Request/Response, URL, Web Streams, AbortController work the same everywhere.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One API","Handler","Adapter"],"captions":["fetch, Request/Response, URL, Web Streams, AbortController, EventTarget — everywhere","(Request) → Response: one handler plugs into any server","Hide platform parts (files, processes) behind an adapter; swap it with the runtime"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"browser","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Node","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Deno / Bun","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":240.0,"h":40.0,"text":"fetch  Request  Response  URL","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["export default async function (req) {","  const url = new URL(req.url);","  return Response.json({ path: url.pathname });","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"app\ncode","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"adapter","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"f","x1":222.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"fs Node / Deno","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.0,26.0]}]},{"title":"node:test","sub":"Built-in test runner","short":"node:test","main":"node:test: test(), describe(), assert — no external libraries; run with node --test.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["test and assert","describe","Running"],"captions":["test(name, fn) and assert — no external libraries","describe groups; it is a synonym of test inside a group","node --test finds *.test.js files and prints a report; --watch reruns"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["import test from \"node:test\";","import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";","","test(\"adds\", () => {","  assert.equal(1 + 1, 2);","});"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["describe(\"cart\", () => {","  it(\"empty\", () => { … });","  it(\"with item\", () => { … });","});"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ node --test","✔ adds (1 ms)","✖ divides by zero","# pass 1   # fail 1"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.4,24.8]}]},{"title":"A good test","sub":"Arrange, Act, Assert","short":"Structure","main":"Arrange, act, assert; tests are independent, an async test waits for its promise.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three parts","Independence","Async"],"captions":["Arrange → act → assert; one test, one idea","Run order does not affect the result: data is created fresh","An async test returns a promise or uses await — otherwise the runner won't wait"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Arrange","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Act","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Assert","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"one array\nfor all tests ✗","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"beforeEach →\nfresh data ✓","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["test(\"loads\", async () => {","  const r = await load();","  assert.equal(r.ok, true);","});"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.5,27.0]}]},{"title":"Mocks and timers","sub":"mock.fn and fake timers","short":"Mocks","main":"mock.fn records calls; fake timers control time without waiting.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["mock.fn","mock.method","Fake timers"],"captions":["mock.fn() records calls and arguments; sets return values","mock.method(obj, \"name\") replaces a method; restore() brings back the original","mock.timers: tick(1000) fires timers with no real waiting"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["const f = mock.fn(() => 42);","f(1, 2);","assert.equal(f.mock.callCount(), 1);","assert.deepEqual(f.mock.calls[0].arguments, [1, 2]);"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["mock.method(api, \"get\", async () => ({ ok: 1 }));","…","api.get.mock.restore();"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["mock.timers.enable({ apis: [\"setTimeout\"] });","setTimeout(done, 5000);","mock.timers.tick(5000);   // fired instantly"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.7,25.5]}]},{"title":"Case tables","sub":"Parameterized tests","short":"Tables","main":"One test over an \"input → expected\" table: a new case is one row.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Table","Loop","Cases to break it"],"captions":["An \"input → expected\" array instead of ten copies of a test","A loop creates a test per row; the name is built from the case data","Add empty input, huge numbers and unexpected types"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["const cases = [","  [\"1\", 1], [\"-5\", -5], [\"0x10\", 16],","];"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["for (const [input, want] of cases) {","  test(`parse(${input})`, () => {","    assert.equal(parse(input), want);","  });","}"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":19.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"\" empty","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1e309","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":295.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"null","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.9,23.8]}]},{"title":"Coverage and CI","sub":"What coverage shows","short":"Coverage","main":"Coverage shows that code ran, not that it was checked.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["What it shows","Not everything","Threshold"],"captions":["Coverage: which lines, branches and functions ran during the tests","Running a line and checking nothing still counts as \"covered\"","CI threshold: below it the build fails; judge quality by other signs too"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"lines 91%","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"branches 78%","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":290.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"functions 95%","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"line ran\nno check","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"100% coverage ≠\ncode checked","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["node --test --experimental-test-coverage","  --test-coverage-lines=80","# build fails if below 80%"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.4,24.7]}]},{"title":"Benchmarks","sub":"Measure honestly","short":"Benchmarks","main":"Warm-up, many repetitions, median and spread; one measurement means nothing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Warm-up","Repeats and median","Conditions"],"captions":["First runs are slower: the engine is still optimizing — discard them","Many repetitions; median and spread beat the mean; monotonic clock","Compare only runs under the same conditions: machine, load, version"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":40.0,"h":10